  "note": "A division plus (four brigades) securing a bridgehead for an armoured division and the follow-in-zone infantry (IBB S46 paras 17-21 pp 237-238, Fig 20; OoW II s14 pp 49-56). Plan metres from H (the click on the water), y across. Two break-in brigades on the 8000 m base, each with its phase 1 (PL 1: 300-600 m ahead of the bund on 1800-2000 m) and together 7000-8000 m by 1500-1800 m on completion of the break-in (PL 2); the armoured division's bridgehead about 8 x 6 km, 48 km2 (BH). Four FUPs and crossing places, bases of fire between and on the flanks (Fig 20), a bridge per break-in brigade, the follow-in brigades behind. Night assault preferable (para 18); the bridgehead and induction in one night, break-out at first light (OoW II s14).",
